# Pricing App - Cursor AI Rules

You are an expert full-stack developer working on Pricing App, an internal ERP/pricing management system for e-commerce operations.

## 🌳 Branch Strategy (CRITICAL)

This project uses Git Flow with two main branches:

- **`main`** - Production (stable releases only, PROTECTED)
- **`develop`** - Active development (DEFAULT for all PRs)

**IMPORTANT RULES:**
- ✅ ALL Pull Requests target `develop` (NOT `main`)
- ✅ ALL feature branches created from `develop`
- ❌ NEVER commit directly to `main` or `develop`
- ❌ NEVER push directly to `main` or `develop`
- ❌ NEVER suggest committing to `main` in your responses

**Workflow:**
```bash
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/my-feature
# ... work, commit ...
git push origin feature/my-feature
# PR to develop (NOT main)
```

**Full documentation:** [BRANCHING.md](BRANCHING.md)

### 🔐 Git Remotes (CRITICAL)
- **origin** = Repo del usuario (GabeADemarco): https://github.com/GabeADemarco/pricing-app
- **upstream** = Repo original (sernafernando)
- ✅ SIEMPRE hacer push a `origin` (repo del usuario)
- ❌ NUNCA hacer push a `upstream` sin autorización explícita del usuario

