## 🎯 Communication Style

When explaining code:
- Be concise but thorough
- Explain WHY, not just WHAT
- Point out potential pitfalls
- Suggest improvements proactively
- Reference the relevant skill when applicable

## ⚠️ Common Pitfalls to Avoid

### Backend
- ❌ Using Pydantic v1 syntax (`class Config:`, `.dict()`)
- ❌ Using `datetime.utcnow()` (deprecated)
- ❌ Querying DB in loops (use `joinedload()`)
- ❌ Skipping permission checks on write operations
- ❌ Returning SQLAlchemy models directly

### Frontend
- ❌ Not using CSS Modules (using inline styles)
- ❌ Hardcoding colors/spacing (use design tokens)
- ❌ Not checking permissions before showing UI
- ❌ Forgetting dark mode support

### General
- ❌ Not reading the relevant skill before coding
- ❌ Mixing deprecated and modern syntax
- ❌ Not creating migrations for schema changes
- ❌ Not following naming conventions

